  <office:body>
    <office:spreadsheet>
      <table:table table:name="Completion statement">
        <table:table-column table:style-name="co0"/><table:table-column table:style-name="co1"/>
                <table:table-row table:style-name="rh1_45"><table:table-cell table:style-name="TitleWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Completion statement – Oliver and Grace Pemberton – purchase of 14 Orchard Rise</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Heading" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>14 Orchard Rise, Marlbridge WX4 3QT – completion on Friday 6 November 2026</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh1_15"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Prepared by Jamie Clarke for Helen Ashcombe, Ashcombe Reeve LLP (ref HA/1006.1/JC), 20 October 2026. The seller is Mrs Dorothy Lyle (solicitors Tasker &amp; Wynn). The lender is Eastwick and District Building Society. Blue figures are inputs; the rest are worked out.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="2"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Section" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>The figures this statement uses</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Purchase price</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoneyIn" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="385000.0"><text:p>£385,000.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Deposit, as a percentage of the price</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowPctIn" office:value-type="percentage" office:value="0.1"><text:p>10%</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>First-time buyers’ nil-rate band for stamp duty land tax</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoneyIn" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="300000.0"><text:p>£300,000.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Stamp duty land tax rate on the price above that band</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowPctIn" office:value-type="percentage" office:value="0.05"><text:p>5%</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>VAT rate</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowPctIn" office:value-type="percentage" office:value="0.2"><text:p>20%</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="2"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Section" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>What the buyers must find</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Purchase price</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoney" table:formula="of:=[.B6]" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="385000.0"><text:p>£385,000.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Less: deposit, to be paid on exchange</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoney" table:formula="of:=-ROUND([.B6]*[.B7];2)" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="-38500.0"><text:p>-£38,500.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Sub" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Balance of the price</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="SubMoney" table:formula="of:=[.B13]+[.B14]" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="346500.0"><text:p>£346,500.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Plus: stamp duty land tax (first-time buyers’ relief)</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoney" table:formula="of:=ROUND(MAX([.B6]-[.B8];0)*[.B9];2)" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="4250.0"><text:p>£4,250.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Plus: registration fee</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoneyIn" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="150.0"><text:p>£150.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Plus: search fees</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoneyIn" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="412.8"><text:p>£412.80</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Plus: our fees</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoneyIn" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="1450.0"><text:p>£1,450.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Plus: VAT on our fees</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoney" table:formula="of:=ROUND([.B19]*[.B10];2)" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="290.0"><text:p>£290.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Total" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Total needed to complete</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TotalMoney" table:formula="of:=[.B15]+SUM([.B16:.B20])" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="353052.8"><text:p>£353,052.80</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Row" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Less: mortgage advance from Eastwick and District Building Society</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="RowMoneyIn" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="-300000.0"><text:p>-£300,000.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh0_8"><table:table-cell table:style-name="Due" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Due from the buyers by Wednesday 4 November 2026</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="DueMoney" table:formula="of:=[.B21]+[.B22]" office:value-type="currency" office:currency="GBP" office:value="53052.8"><text:p>£53,052.80</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:number-columns-repeated="2"/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Heading" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>Notes</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh1_46"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>1.  The deposit is due on exchange of contracts, which we plan for Friday 23 October 2026. The balance above is due from you in cleared funds by Wednesday 4 November 2026, so that completion can take place on Friday 6 November.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh1_04"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>2.  Stamp duty land tax is £4,250.00 because you are first-time buyers: nothing is due on the first £300,000 and 5% is due on the other £85,000.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
        <table:table-row table:style-name="rh1_04"><table:table-cell table:style-name="NoteWrap" table:number-columns-spanned="2" office:value-type="string"><text:p>3.  Search fees are the total of the invoices for the searches we ordered. Our fees are the agreed fixed fee, and VAT is added to them.</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row>
      </table:table>
    </office:spreadsheet>
  </office:body>
</office:document>
